the fbi is investigating the discovery  of a noose in the garage  of nascar's only african-american driver  it is believed to be part of the fallout  from the organization's recent ban  of confederate symbols which is a  growing movement throughout the country  correspondent kevin cork has details  it was a powerful symbol solidarity and  unwavering fidelity for both sport  and driver it was all in support of  nascar driver bubba wallace  the sport's lone african-american driver  whose garage  was the scene of an apparent despicable  act on sunday  a noose discovered near his team garage  a warning or perhaps  a reminder of a violent and forgettable  past etched into america's fabric  that noose was found by a member of his  team just hours after someone  blew a confederate flag over alabama's  talladega super speedway  to protest nascar banning the symbol at  all events  and while views on the flag issue are  mixed among nascar fans  support for wallace in the wake of the  noose incident was resounding  richard petty seven-time nascar champion  affectionately known as the king  said there's absolutely no place in our  sport or society for racism  adding this filthy act serves as a  reminder of how far we still have to go  lebron james tweeted his support to  wallace i just want to continue to say  how proud i am of you  for continuing to take a stand for  change here in america  and sports wallace has created some  controversy with nascar fans  thanks to his vocal support of the black  lives matter movement and to be clear  while both nascar and the fbi are  investigating this incident  there's still much we don't know about  what's alleged to have happened  including what did surveillance cameras  capture and who had access or  opportunity  it's all part of an increasingly  complicated portrait  of a country re-examining its past and  pondering its future  and nowhere is that more evident than  outside the american museum of natural  history in new york  where a statue of former president teddy  roosevelt is now in queue to be removed  over concerns of its reflection of  racism and imperialism  and right there was this from dale  earnhardt jr on twitter he said i hope  bubba  is feeling loved and supported keep  sending him that love and support  he needs it now more than ever brett  kevin thank you
 

